  "body": "### What happens\nA refused post (gouge, travel limits, a post-script warning such as #170's rigid-tap refusal on the Tormach 770M) writes no file, and the reason goes **only to the status line** (`crates/ui/src/state.rs` `post_program_path`: `self.status = format!(\"post refused: {err}\")`). The status line is shared with hover text, so moving the mouse over the viewport replaces the reason at once (\"no model under the cursor\").\n\nFound while testing PR #259 in the GUI: posting a tap job on the Tormach 770M produced no file and, as far as the user could see, **no message anywhere**. The refusal was there (pinned by `a_tap_job_posts_on_the_1100mx_and_is_refused_on_the_770m`), but it lived only for the instant before the next hover.\n\n### Why it matters\nPrime Directive: the output is either correct or **visibly** refused with a diagnostic. A refusal the user can't see looks like the Post button silently doing nothing.\n\n### Suggested fix\nKeep a post refusal on screen until the user dismisses it: a small modal or a sticky error banner with the full text (the gouge and limit lists can be long), and/or a refusal entry in the PostView pane. Hover text should never overwrite it. A UI test: a refused post leaves the reason visible after a hover update.\n\nSuggested labels (the filer can't set labels): `bug`, `P1`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
